<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0">
  <head><title>Session prep and the blank page (Pointliner demo)</title></head>
  <body>
    <outline text="# Session prep and the blank page" _id="prep0001">
      <outline text="How to start a solo session and capture ideas mid-play without breaking flow. This case is mostly about three built-in doors you click rather than type: TEMPLATES (stamp a fresh session), CAPTURE (log a mid-play idea without leaving your place), and JOURNAL mode (today's dated entry). The few {…} pills here are live, click one to run it. See session-prep.md for the walkthrough." _id="prep0002"/>
      <outline text="## The blank page problem" _id="prep0010">
        <outline text="A solo session starts by staring at nothing. What is the scene? What is unresolved? What might interrupt me? Two habits fix the blank page: keep a fixed session structure you stamp fresh each time (a TEMPLATE), and keep one place to dump ideas so a stray thought never derails the current scene (a CAPTURE inbox that feeds an inbox point)." _id="prep0011"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## A Session template (the thing you stamp)" _id="prep0020">
        <outline text="This subtree is the shape of one session. Save a subtree like this as a template from its bullet menu (Save as template), or with /savetemplate:session, and it lives on the document. At the start of each play session you stamp a fresh copy with /template:session (or bare /template to pick from a list). Below is the template filled in as an example so you can see what a stamped session looks like." _id="prep0021"/>
        <outline text="Session 2026-07-04" _id="prep0030">
          <outline text="Scene seeds (where could we open?): a knock at the door, a debt comes due, the map is wrong." _id="prep0031"/>
          <outline text="Threads to chase (what is still open from last time): the torn letter, the merchant's back room, who paid the informant." _id="prep0032"/>
          <outline text="Oracle on hand (is it so?): {Yes 6 | No 6}. Click to ask, click again to re-ask." _id="prep0033"/>
          <outline text="Session-start event (draw one to open the scene): {shuffle: complication | ally appears | clock ticks | quiet}. A deck, so it draws each once before it reshuffles." _id="prep0034"/>
          <outline text="Random event roll (mid-session, when the fiction stalls): {2d6}. On a 10 or more, something intrudes." _id="prep0035"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## Capture: a mid-play inbox" _id="prep0040">
        <outline text="The toolbar inbox button (or Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+I) toggles the capture strip open below the toolbar, with the document still visible underneath, so it never navigates you off the current scene. Each capture appends one point to the end of a chosen inbox. Nothing is set up in this demo, and nothing has to be: with no inbox chosen, captures land at the top level of the document. To send them here instead, pick Set as inbox 1 from this point's bullet menu, then mid-scene, when an idea strikes, capture it and keep playing. Refile it into its scene later (bullet menu Refile, or /refile:TITLE)." _id="prep0041">
          <outline text="Captured: the merchant's cousin runs the ferry, could be the informant." _id="prep0042"/>
          <outline text="Captured: name for the abbey on the ridge, the Ashfast." _id="prep0043"/>
          <outline text="Captured: a clock for the flood, three segments." _id="prep0044"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## Journal mode: today's play entry" _id="prep0050">
        <outline text="The /journal verb (or the journal block command) opens today's entry. It finds or creates a Journal home point at the TOP LEVEL of the document, then nests the date under it as year, then month, then day, so each play session is one dated point and the entries stack in date order on their own. The toolbar journal button is a different door: it toggles the journal strip, a bar you type into, and its date chips are what navigate. This is the built-in version of what the Lonelog case does by hand. The Journal home sits at the bottom of this document, outside this branch, because that is where the door actually creates it." _id="prep0051"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## How to run it" _id="prep0070">
        <outline text="Stamp a session: save the Session subtree above as a template (its bullet menu, Save as template), then run /template:session on an empty point to drop a fresh copy in. A new session structure in one command, no blank page." _id="prep0071"/>
        <outline text="Set the inbox and capture: open a point's bullet menu and pick Set as inbox 1 (try the Capture inbox point above). Then click the toolbar inbox button, type an idea, press Enter. It lands as the last point inside the inbox and the strip stays open for the next one, you never leave your scene." _id="prep0072"/>
        <outline text="Open today's entry: type /journal. It takes you to today's point under the Journal home, nested year, then month, then day, creating each rung if it does not exist yet. The toolbar journal button opens the journal strip instead, where you type an entry or click a date chip to jump. One dated entry per session, built in." _id="prep0073"/>
        <outline text="Refile a capture: on a captured point, open the bullet menu and pick Refile (or type /refile:TITLE), then choose the scene it belongs under. The idea moves out of the inbox and into the fiction where it lives." _id="prep0074"/>
        <outline text="Run a pill: click {Yes 6 | No 6} to ask the oracle, {shuffle: complication | ally appears | clock ticks | quiet} to draw a session-start event, or {2d6} for a random event roll. Each freezes its result, click again to re-run." _id="prep0075"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  <outline text="Journal" _id="prep0060">
  <outline text="2026" _id="prep0065">
    <outline text="07" _id="prep0066">
      <outline text="04" _id="prep0061">
        <outline text="&gt; I open on a knock at the door, the debt come to collect. Oracle, is the collector alone? {Yes 6 | No 6}." _id="prep0062"/>
        <outline text="=&gt; Two of them at the door. I stall and reach for the ledger. Random event to see if the scene turns: {2d6}." _id="prep0063"/>
        <outline text="=&gt; Idea mid-scene, captured to the inbox so I can keep the beat moving, refile it after: the cousin on the ferry." _id="prep0064"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body>
</opml>
